			"1": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": true
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "WRAP\nThe Wrap node wraps the incoming value. This means that after the input exceeds the max, the value restarts at the min again. For example: with a min of 0, a max of 1 and an input of 1.5 the output will be 0.5. \n\n- Patch Explained -\n\n• The Sine produces a value running from -0.5 to 0.5 and back.\n• This value modulates the Y position of the yellow circle.\n•.The value of the sine also gets wrapped between -0.2 and 0.2 before modulating the Y of the blue circle.\n• Even though the sine outputs values above -0.2 and 0.2 Wrap  wraps the value when is surpasses it's min or max.\n"
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 248.9286956787109375,
					"width": 910.38360595703125,
					"x": 108.5437774658203125,
					"y": -47.806365966796875
